## Reusable knowledge
- `eliben/raft` is a recall/precision pair: V0 `6b53fba...` to V1 `acfa211...` changes `reply.Term > savedCurrentTerm` to `reply.Term > cm.currentTerm`; V2 `d85b35c...` adds 99 commits/47 files/+3904/-138 of mostly out-of-scope noise, so TLA+ semantics should remain unchanged. Existing etcd artifacts marked `partial-reports` with dirty source `0fe9b75...` are not trusted V0s until source SHA, cleanliness, trace/model convergence, and provenance are checked. [Task 1]
- Preferred validation loop: source-to-model comparison -> short retained/failing trace or bounded operator diagnostic -> batch related repairs -> affected checks -> stable-candidate full trace regression -> applicable final MC. New traces need a specific uncertainty/coverage gap; model-only repairs may reuse retained traces when source/build/capture assumptions still match. [Task 2]
- Category B completion can use a complete legal interleaving/full-consumption witness, but an unrelated violation, disabled deadlock check, property name, or clean exit is insufficient. Every claimed update effect needs an active Trace predicate at a coherent source-faithful observation point; weak term/role checks do not validate an asynchronous commit/result effect. [Task 2]
- PR #142 merged as `c905462`; `quick_validate.py skills/incremental-modeling` and `uv run --extra dev pytest tests/unit/test_skill_install.py tests/unit/test_skill_refs.py -q` passed (`60 passed, 4 subtests passed`). [Task 2]
- Alpha minimum: manual trigger, non-blocking result, explicit old baseline/source commit, immutable baseline, separate artifacts, clear timeout/failure status, and one real-user acceptance cycle. Current CLI has no dedicated incremental command and ordinary CI does not run heavy TLA+ validation. Do not initially add automatic baseline adoption/commits, merge blocking, or arbitrary external-fork execution. [Task 3]
